 We can write the equation as
\[\sin^5 x - \cos^5 x = \frac{\sin x - \cos x}{\sin x \cos x},\]so
\[\sin^5 x - \cos^5 x - \frac{\sin x - \cos x}{\sin x \cos x} = 0.\]Then乘 up by $\sin x \cos x$,
\[\sin^6 x \cos x - \cos^6 x - (\sin x - \cos x) = 0.\]Note that $\sin^2 x - 2 \sin x \cos x + \cos^2 x = (\sin x - \cos x)^2 = Z^2$ (where $Z$ is some real number), so this equation is equivalent to
\[Z^6 - Z = 0.\]Hence, $Z(Z^5 - 1) = 0$, so either $Z = 0$ or $Z^5 = 1$.

In the case $Z = 0$, $\sin x = \cos x$, so $x = 45^\circ,$ $135^\circ,$ $225^\circ,$ and $315^\circ$.

In the case $Z^5 = 1$, either $\sin x = \cos x$ or $Z = 1.$  If $Z = 1,$ then
\[\sin^6 x - \cos^6 x - (\sin x - \cos x) = 0,\]and $Z^6 = 1$, so $x = 0^\circ,$ $Z = 2 \pi,$ $Z = 4 \pi,$ etc.  We leave it to the reader to solve this equation.  (One idea is to rewrite everything in terms of $\tan x$ by dividing both sides by $\cos^6 x$.)

